---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { skills, credentials } from '../data/site';
---
<Layout title="About — Javier Ponz" description="Background, experience, skills and credentials of Javier Ponz.">
<section class="hero"><p class="kicker">About</p><h1>People, systems, <span class="serif">service</span>.</h1><p class="lede">My work lives at the boundary: diagnose what is wrong, understand who is affected, explain the trade-offs, and leave the system working better than I found it.</p></section>
<section class="grid"><span class="label">Experience</span><div class="copy"><h2>Apple Retail · 2014—2024</h2><p>I moved through Specialist, Technical Specialist, AppleCare Advisor, Genius and In-Store Experience Lead across Parquesur and Xanadú in Madrid. The common thread was diagnosis under pressure: find the real failure, explain it in terms the person actually cares about, and keep trust intact while doing it.</p><p>As In-Store Experience Lead I ran operations across two stores — opening and closing routines, events, resourcing, maintenance coordination, and supporting teams when the situation did not fit a procedure. Ten years in a high-standards environment shaped how I think about reliability, documentation and execution.</p></div></section>
<section class="grid"><span class="label">Now</span><div class="copy"><h2>AI systems and full stack</h2><p>Since moving to Aberdeen I have been building AI systems full time: agent workflows with OpenClaw and Hermes Agent, MCP servers, automation pipelines, and applications deployed on my own VPS with Docker, Traefik and TLS. I am strongest where systems fail — investigating failure modes, debugging workflows, and turning messy behaviour into something predictable and documented.</p><p>I am early in this career, and deliberately public about it: every project here has source code, tests and a stated scope. I would rather be judged on what I have shipped than on how I describe myself.</p></div></section>
<section class="grid"><span class="label">Skills</span><div class="copy">{Object.entries(skills).map(([group, items]) => <div class="skillgroup"><h3>{group}</h3><div class="tags">{items.map((item) => <span class="tag">{item}</span>)}</div></div>)}</div></section>
<section class="grid"><span class="label">Credentials</span><div class="rows">{credentials.map((c) => <article class="row"><time>{c.date}</time><div><h3>{c.title}</h3><p>{c.org}{c.org && c.status ? ' · ' : ''}{c.status}</p></div></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="grid"><span class="label">Principle</span><div class="notice">Leading is serving. Good technical work leaves people with more clarity and more control.</div></section>
</Layout>
